# StickLLM hard blocklist (v0.5.3; ComfyUI unblocked in v0.5.4). One app id per line, then the reason.
# These apps are never listed (kiosk, LAN UI, /api/apps, Agent Zero) and every
# install path refuses them server-side. scripts/pins.py copies this list into
# verified.json ("blocked_apps"); stickllm_verify.BLOCKED_APPS must match it.
# Unblocking needs Nink's decision, a pin, an add-on definition and tests.

paperless-ngx        Needs Redis plus OCR worker containers; StickLLM add-ons are one locked-down container each.
snappymail           Webmail needs outbound IMAP/SMTP, and add-on containers have no network by design.
immich               Needs Postgres, Redis and a machine-learning container (four containers) plus a GPU for search.
searxng              Already built into Agent Zero (its own private search); a second copy adds nothing.
matrix               Federation and bridges need internet and LAN access; add-on containers have no network.
simplex              Relay servers only, used from phone and desktop apps; nothing to open in a browser tab.
jitsi                Four containers including the Java video bridge, and calls need LAN/internet UDP.
onionshare           Command line plus Tor, which needs internet; no web app to open.
postiz               Node, Postgres and Redis, and posting needs internet access to the social networks.
opentimestamps       Command-line tools with no web app; timestamping needs internet calendars.
code-server-jupyter  Not packaged and security-reviewed for the stick yet (a full terminal and package installs).
n8n                  Fair-code licence (not OSI open source) and it duplicates Node-RED, which ships.
